California Housing Price Prediction

Project Overview

This project uses machine learning regression algorithms to predict median house values in California based on housing and geographical features.

A Streamlit application allows users to enter housing details and receive an estimated median house value.

Dataset

•⁠  ⁠Dataset: California Housing
•⁠  ⁠Number of records: 20,640
•⁠  ⁠Features: 8
•⁠  ⁠Target: MedHouseVal
•⁠  ⁠Target values are measured in units of $100,000.

Machine Learning Algorithms

Three regression algorithms were trained and evaluated:

1.⁠ ⁠Linear Regression
2.⁠ ⁠Decision Tree Regressor
3.⁠ ⁠Random Forest Regressor

Evaluation Metrics

The models were evaluated using:

•⁠  ⁠Mean Absolute Error (MAE)
•⁠  ⁠Mean Squared Error (MSE)
•⁠  ⁠Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE)
•⁠  ⁠R² Score

